# MindPalace environment overrides.
#
# Runtime settings live in config/settings.toml. The variables below are the
# only environment overrides the code reads (src/palace/llm/client.py), and they
# win over settings.toml. Nothing loads a .env file automatically: export them in
# your shell (e.g. `set -a; source .env; set +a`) before running `palace`.
#
# Use these for per-machine model choices instead of editing settings.toml.
# The spec (docs/mindpalace-master-specification.md, section 1) lists
# qwen3:14b as the reasoning-tier default; a smaller model is a local override
# for machines that cannot run it.

# Fast tier: claim extraction. Default: llm.fast_tier_model (qwen3:4b).
# PALACE_LLM_FAST_MODEL=qwen3:4b

# Reasoning tier: chat replies and `palace compile`. Default: llm.reasoning_tier_model.
# PALACE_LLM_REASONING_MODEL=qwen2.5:7b

# How long Ollama keeps a model loaded between requests. Default: 10m.
# PALACE_OLLAMA_KEEP_ALIVE=10m

# The Ollama endpoint is NOT an environment variable; change llm.ollama_host and
# embedding.ollama_host in config/settings.toml.
